# design-sync (claude.ai/design) — transient build + verification state

#Design Sync Exports for UI changes and New Feature UI

# Okta demo-org seeding (seed/) — these hold real org identifiers and must not
# be committed: data/ is the exported group/rule/app CSVs, .state/ records the
# ids of users a run created. The script itself is safe to commit; it reads the
# org URL and API token from the environment only.
seed/data/
seed/.state/

# Demo reel: shot footage and the composition workspace.
# Clips are large and reproducible from `npm run capture`.
# Rendered output: stills and encodes, hundreds of MB, all reproducible from
# `npm run still` / `npm run render`. `out/` is Remotion's default and fills up
# fast during a judging pass, which is exactly when nobody is watching git.

# Demo reel: the CommonJS build `emit-plan.mjs` compiles into and deletes.

# publish/: the replay is deterministic, so the SHA map is a local speed
# optimisation only. Never commit it — a stale map is worse than none.
publish/shamap.json
